WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.780
Who's my next patient?

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.980
My room?

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.060
How am I back here?

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.900
I remember there was an outbreak 
in the village to the west...

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.110
It's a contagious disease.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.190
Medicine could treat it,

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.540
but they don't have the money to buy it.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.040
We don't need no medicine, Doctor.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.370
I'll cure them all with magic!

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.640
You woke up?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.970
Give your thanks to the physician.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.650
He carried you on his back 
after you passed out.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.230
I passed out?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.890
You were magically depleted. 
You tried to heal all 13 at once.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.850
You ran out of magic partway through.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.810
That makes me look lame!

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.300
You missed out.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.100
If you had been conscious, 
you could have eaten Lilly's cooking.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.280
Lilly's?

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.840
Why was she cooking? 
Did the old mercenary die?

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.930
Sorry. I didn't mean to bring it back up.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.800
I-It's fine. What happened 
to him was my fault.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.950
You killed him?!

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.580
No! I just accidentally 
hit him with a spell!

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.230
So you tried to kill him?

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.800
Shut up! An edge-lizord who ran out 
of magic has no room to criticize!

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.730
Wow, Hort, that's really funny.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.260
"Edge-lizord?!"

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.090
Why, you! I'll kill you even if it kills me!

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.660
Be quiet!

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.860
What possesses thee to shout a thing 
like "I'll kill you" at night?

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.660
Wh-Why're <i>you</i> here? 
Did ya come to lecture us?

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.160
Well, we all really messed up today.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.310
Yeah. I got lost in the forest with Laios.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.380
Indeed. So tell me.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:59.110
How do you all intend
 to face your deeds?

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:06.840
I won't use magic in actual combat 
until I learn how to stop a spell.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.530
I'll... only use magic for emergency 
cases and consult my boss for the rest.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.520
Consult? Thou meanest "seek his wisdom."

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.070
If thou wishest to talk a big game, 
put in the work first.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.540
D-Don't call me an edge-lizord!

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.990
Now you, Sayb.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.030
I'll start by leaving the house.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.980
I promised to play with Laios 
in the forest tomorrow,

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.960
but I asked his parents' permission.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.130
Very well.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.810
But if thou art going into the forest, 
collect medicinal herbs.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.710
It shall double as a herbology lesson.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.530
Isn't Saybil getting off easy?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.830
Nope.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.120
G-Get off me! You're heavy!

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:58.590
Well, it seems you three know what to do,

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.690
but you ought to go see the Mud-Black 
Witch together tomorrow.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.700
Huh? But what about work?

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.220
No one will die if you 
three take one day off.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.000
Have a good day!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.010
Episode 7   "I Can't Save Anything"

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.750
You, too, Professor! We're off!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.010
Professor Los is kinda like a mom!

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.630
Is that what moms are like?

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:59.190
She's not like my mom, 
but she's strict yet kind.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.890
And she's helpful and reliable.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.270
<i>A mom...</i>

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.760
This is an incredible number of books.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.580
This collection is the limited 
fraction of books I keep on hand.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.600
Most go to the Forbidden Library.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.830
The Forbidden Library?

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.470
Niedora Fort. In the north.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:19.090
You're from the north, right, Kudo?

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.950
Have you ever been there?

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.990
Of course not. Duh.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.100
The Forbidden Library isn't on maps,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.470
since it's where they keep books 
the Church has forbidden.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:34.430
Thus, it's set up so you can't get 
close if you don't know where it is.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.790
Amazing!

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.900
I'm definitely gonna go someday.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.800
Hey, let's all go together!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.680
Sure.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.550
That's a hell no from me.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.840
The north is crawling with 
Remnants of Disaster.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.040
You'll be killed in the blink of an eye.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.560
Are these "Remnants of
 Disaster" that dangerous?

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.150
Well...

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.260
If you encounter one while unprepared,

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.210
you'll either die tragically or 
suffer so much, you'll wish you had.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.130
Maybe I don't really want to go, either.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:07.210
Don't worry! I'll protect both of you!

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:14.990
If you supply magical energy and Kudo heals, 
then, ta-dah! We're unstoppable!

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.440
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.450
A mage who nearly kills her party members

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.800
and a medical mage who passes out mid-heal.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.850
I-I'm gonna learn proper control!

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.550
Regarding that,

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:32.350
antlered girl, I have a 
special lesson for you.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:37.030
You won't be released until 
you can cancel your spells.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:44.140
Ahh! I'm sorry! I'm sorry I 
hit Mercenary! Forgive me!

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.110
Find a good book?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.500
Yeah. I think so.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.010
Flagis! My name is Hort!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.180
Disappear!

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.140
Hmm. Not too bad. This will do.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.200
That was a close one.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.670
Keep honing your skills like that.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:16.050
As an exercise, I recommend using Flagis 
to light all the candles in your home.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.610
I-I don't have enough magic for that!

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.940
That just now was my expenditure 
for one cast of Flagis.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:36.150
The way to cast from your textbook 
is ultimately just one example.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.380
Try applying it in different ways.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.390
Even if you expend too much magical energy,

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:42.920
you have a supplier—

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.060
P-Professor Zero!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.500
Professor Zero!

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.610
I-I'm fine.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.480
I'm just slightly depleted.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.350
B-But...

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.400
Hey...

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.290
Huh?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.460
The magic transfer isn't working.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.670
Maybe via the lips, like yesterday?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.500
L-Lips?!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:12.930
It's fine.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.660
More importantly, I'm hungry.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.980
I'll feel a little better once I eat...

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.830
Amazing, Sayb!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:22.850
You're so strong!

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:29.180
Could you two go to Mercenary and 
bring some food back from the bar?

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.840
You got it!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.590
I'll carry Professor Zero inside.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.610
It's still not working.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.570
Why?

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.170
You have nothing to worry about. Try to stab 
me through the heart with this knife.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.930
Even if I said that, most people 
couldn't bring themselves to try.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.910
I could probably fully rob you of magic.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.700
I'm a natural enemy to you.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.850
<i>The same color as mine...</i>

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.330
Your eyes

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.530
are the same as mine, young man.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.080
Professor Zero.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.100
My mother...

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.390
do you know her?

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.680
No.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.970
Your father, on the other hand...

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.090
My father...

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.540
Oh, right. I have a father, too.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.580
That book. Did you take it from my library?

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.660
Oh, yes.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.500
I'm going into the forest today, so I 
wanted a book about medicinal herbs.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:40.650
The penmanship is terrible, 
isn't it? Extraordinarily so.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:43.510
It took me a lot of effort to decipher it.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:48.090
Not at all. My handwriting is similar, 
so it's easy to understand.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:49.660
I see.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.270
I'm sure the author would 
be upset to hear that.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:10:00.500
Witches employ tricks to prevent others 
from using the knowledge in their books.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.200
What? Does that include <i>this</i> book?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.410
However, I failed to discover any tricks.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:12.590
After all, the medicines are plenty effective 
if you follow the book's instructions exactly.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:18.110
They're that effective, and yet to 
the author, they're still defective.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:20.560
That's the sort of information 
written in that tome.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.910
It's an incredible book.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.570
What sort of witch wrote it, I wonder?

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.380
A sorcerer.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.190
Huh?

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:31.980
It was a sorcerer who wrote that 
book. In other words, a man.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.280
You mean it was my father?

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.150
He was a sorcerer with unparalleled talent.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:44.240
Always calm, deeply inquisitive, 
and totally unshakable.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.090
Wow. I'm not like him at all.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.610
Actually, it would be a 
big deal if you were.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.820
Still, you described that 
book as "easy to understand."

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:58.020
Perhaps <i>you'll</i> uncover the book's secrets.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.930
It would appear he came.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.500
Mercenary? That was fast.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:09.230
He must have run here full bore 
the moment he was informed,

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:14.490
but paused to catch his breath, and now
 intentionally ascends the stairs slowly.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.550
That's just how he is.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.620
Hey, there. You're looking 
better than I expected.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.830
Wh-What?

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.360
What're you looking at?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.730
Do I spy smoked pork? And sausage, too!

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:33.200
Sorry. Thanks for staying with her.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.810
It was nothing. Sorry I couldn't 
supply her with magic,

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:38.710
even though it's my job.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:41.270
Listen. About that...

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:42.710
Wait, Mercenary.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.290
I'll say it.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.090
Young man, you...

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:52.610
So, for those tea leaves, you're looking for 
a red flower blooming at the base of a tree.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.390
Sayb!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:55.990
Huh?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.240
You're staring off into space!

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:02.100
Oh, sorry. I had something on my mind.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:05.800
Laios, these mushrooms are edible.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.990
This tree supposedly bears fruit.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:13.450
Laios, stop! Touching that 
will make you itchy.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:14.190
What?

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:18.460
Sayb, you seem really grown-up today!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.970
Huh? I do?

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:23.110
I mean, you can read books because 
you're a grown-up, right?

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:27.130
If you study, you'll be able 
to read soon, too, Laios.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:32.250
Really? You don't just learn 
to read when you grow up?

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.120
No, it doesn't just happen automatically.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.550
Do you want to be a magic supplier?

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.470
Or do you want to be a mage?

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:47.290
I had you three set up shops here 
to further your studies as mages.

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:50.880
If you have no desire to be a mage,

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:53.660
then there is nothing for you to learn here.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.780
I...

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.690
Take some time to think

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.470
about the path you want to take.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.500
A dead animal.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.810
Was it attacked by wolves?

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:10.510
What? Wolves?

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:14.770
But you can beat wolves with 
your magic, right, Sayb?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.500
Uh, no... I...

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:21.100
We made it! Red flowers!

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.980
This has gotta be it, right, Sayb?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.140
Yeah.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.910
Check us out! We found them all on our own!

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.620
We're an adventuring party!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.910
Where should we go tomorrow?

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:38.130
Um...

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.710
What, you don't want to?

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.560
That's not it. It's just that 
I have to practice magic.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.370
Oh. Yeah...

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.810
Grown-ups are busy.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.760
Do you want to go out with 
me while I practice magic?

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.180
So, you'll practice magic with me every day?

00:13:59.180 --> 00:13:59.900
Yep.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.340
Yay!

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.750
Sayb, we're gonna be married!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.450
That's taking it a little far...

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:13.250
Laios, we'd better head ba—

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.370
Sayb?

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.290
Laios,

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.090
get down!

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:45.080
Sayb, I...

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:48.860
Laios!

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.260
Laios, hang on!

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.080
What do I do...

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:00.450
I'm causing problems again...

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.600
Healing magic!

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:05.160
I can't. I've never cast it successfully.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.170
What do I do?

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:15.510
It hurts. It hurts, Sayb.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:21.990
Hang on, Laios.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:24.560
It's gonna be okay.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.650
It hur...

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.300
Laios.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:34.750
Laios!

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.130
His breathing...

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.940
You have to hold on!

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.710
We're almost out of the forest!
 We're almost there!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.740
Why...

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:51.210
Why didn't I practice?

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:54.430
Even the simplest spell would have helped.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:55.950
Somebody!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.650
Professor Los!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.720
Get up, Sayb! Get up!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:10.160
Run! The Mud-Black Witch is on the way.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.910
Laios isn't dead yet! Get up and run!

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.290
Professor Los...

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.270
Gotta make it... Gotta get there in time!

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:41.410
Professor Zero! Mercenary!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.650
I-I'm sorry...

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.170
I...

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.550
failed again...

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.130
Don't be stupid!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.050
You successfully protected him!

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:54.150
You persevered and reached us!

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.920
He's suffering from blood loss...

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.240
Incoming!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.220
Dawn Witch! Give me your blood!

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:02.200
Very well!

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.000
Take it!

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:10.080
I have plenty to give!

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.840
So <i>you</i> collapsed from blood loss,

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:23.400
and <i>you</i> from magic depletion?

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.770
I know I said I had plenty,

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:30.350
but thou didst truly take 
too much all at once.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:32.880
I had to act quickly,

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.690
but you're the one who 
slashed your wrist open!

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:38.830
Shut yer yaps and get some rest!

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:41.700
Saybil, how long are you gonna cry?

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.760
Sorry. It just won't stop...

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.850
You can cry.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:51.250
Just keep letting the tears 
out until they stop.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.360
Then Laios will laugh at hi—

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.060
Huh?

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.140
Where'd he go?

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.040
Get this! Sayb and I

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:02.630
fought a monster!

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:06.150
Then I was gravely wounded protecting him—

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.160
Laios...

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:10.610
D-D-Daddy!

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.690
It must have been a Remnant of Disaster.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:17.650
I saw a very similar illustration 
in a book at the Forbidden Library.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:22.290
It disguises itself as a dead 
animal to lure in prey.

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:26.260
The many barbs it launches suck blood,

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:32.760
and then sprout limbs and climb 
up a tree to await more prey.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:36.750
I believe it was labeled "Touch-Me-Not."

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:41.630
'Tis a plaything demons created 
to torment and kill humans.

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:44.920
They were created in the 
Disasters of the North,

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:49.300
and even with the demons gone, 
they continue to multiply.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:54.290
But the Church & Mage 
Army's line of defense

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.860
ought to prevent them
 from venturing south.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.100
That one suddenly appeared 
in the forest means

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.810
someone set it loose there.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.110
I am exceedingly displeased.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.430
I'll go pay the father a little visit.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.300
I'll go, too.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.500
Stay in bed.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.090
Oh? What're you doin' here, dog-face?

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.980
I'm a wolf!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:26.240
Someone's catching Remnants of 
Disaster and sellin' 'em off?

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:26.720
Yeah.

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:32.260
I thought it was hogwash, but if one was
 in the village, it's a different story.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:34.740
The Church accepted peace with witches.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:41.750
Anyone who seeks to fracture 
 that peace is a heretic.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.480
Time to gather information.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.720
Let's go, Lilly.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.230
Wait, I'm coming, too?

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:51.490
We have a rat to sniff out. 
That's your forte.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.890
But if I leave the village...

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:55.970
Then what?

00:19:55.970 --> 00:20:00.630
Being in the village didn't enable 
you to find the creature.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:05.870
Um, my friends... they're all scared...

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:10.030
They can't get near the thing that 
looks like... a ball of thorns.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:12.740
They can't see it because 
they can't get near it.

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.440
Calm down, little one.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.990
The father isn't blaming you.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:21.100
I got reports that the forest 
creatures were acting strange,

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.550
but I didn't try to find out why.

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.040
I'm at fault, too.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.560
I need to go inform 
the neighboring village.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:32.120
And leave this village with weak defenses?

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.040
This isn't an outsider's business.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.510
I'm here to conduct a surprise inspection.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:41.550
An inspection? Oh, because 
you're incompetent and idle.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.640
Because I'm the <i>most</i> competent!

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.670
That's fine.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:51.380
If we have someone so capable with us,
 we can't let that go to waste.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:54.670
The priest and I are leaving the village.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:59.170
A worn-out witch and the old biddy 
with the staff may not be enough.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:00.850
Please protect them.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.700
You sure you want to leave them to me?

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:07.080
I failed to protect the woman 
who is most important to me.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:14.250
You're not the only one whose regrets and 
failures wake them up at night, dog-face.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.440
If you want to play the tragic hero,

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:21.830
wait until you've killed the one 
you love with your own hands first.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:25.160
What, is this a sob story contest?

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.070
So it's settled.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:29.300
H-Hey!

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:32.180
What are you doing? Go lie down!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:35.610
I knew you were planning to leave me behind.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:40.280
I mean, you're suffering 
from magic depletion.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:44.290
I'm still a witch. I can protect you.

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:48.780
I think you should take the 
Mud-Black Witch with you.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:53.300
We beastfallen are made 
to work with witches.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.960
Can it, dog-face.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.370
Or, rather, if Zero has decided 
to go, we cannot stop her.

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.790
I think you two should stay together!

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:07.180
Mercenary.

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:10.140
It's unanimous. Accept it.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.200
We'll be going now.

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:14.130
W-Wait for me!

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.920
We haven't been to the city in so long!

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.280
We aren't visiting for fun.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:58.610
Did you see? I played a really big part!

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:09.960
<b>Next Episode         "Respective Costs"</b>

00:23:58.610 --> 00:24:01.930
Laios, stay away from Saybil.

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:03.510
What? How come?

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:06.420
Next episode: "Respective Costs."

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.910
Why art <i>thou</i> saying it?!
